/* ================= SPELL TALENTS: how a force's units come by their spells, and talents that shape them =================
   Force runs only (oldRules(): Classic and Tower Wars keep the keep's Lore research and the tier learn points).
   - Every unit is raised knowing ONE spell: its innate ability (kit ability 1 in UNIT_KITS).
   - Its other two spells unlock through its own talent tree, on rows II-IV, never row I or the capstone row (owner, 6 Nov
     2026: "more randomised ... the strength of a spell should be relative to where it sits"; "don't have any on the first
     row"). Each tree places them on purpose (the force files): II and III, II and IV, or III and IV, spell 3 always
     deeper than spell 2; rows open at TAL_TIER points (3, 6, 9). Each spell talent needs the talent straight above it in
     its column at full rank, and the two spells sit in different columns. A talent that shapes a spell sits below that
     spell's talent, the first of them straight below it, so none waits on a spell the player can't have yet. A row IV
     spell's upgrades sit in the capstone row (row V): they are capstones, and a tree takes one capstone.
   - A spell's row sets its strength (SP_DEPTH, below): row II is its kit's own numbers, each row deeper hits harder (or
     lasts longer, for a spell that deals no damage) and costs a little more.
   - A spell talent makes the spell AVAILABLE to the unit type. Each unit then pays gold to learn it, on its card or its
     gear sheet (SP_LEARN_GOLD). The gold counts as invested in the unit (selling refunds it as it refunds upgrades), and
     resetting the tree forgets the spell on every unit and gives that gold back.
   Talents carry sp: n => entry | [entries] (rank n). An entry names one of its unit's spells (ab) and any of:
     cd: -0.1          its cooldown 10% shorter          cost: -0.2      its mana cost 20% lower
     by: { n: 1 }      add to one of the spell's per-tier numbers (ab.by[key], read through byT): more targets, longer holds
     reach: 0.3        cells added to its reach (spells that aim with abReach)
     vs: [cond, k]     its hits deal +k to foes in a state (SP_COND): damage only in tandem with a condition
     rider: { ... }    every foe its hits strike gets this too (SP_RIDE; once per foe per 2s)
     haste: [k, s]     each cast quickens the unit's strikes by k for s seconds
     ally: m           each cast gives m mana to every other unit within 1.6 cells
     every: N          every Nth cast of it gives its mana back
     ready: [id, s]    each cast brings another of its spells s seconds nearer
     kill: { mana, cd }  a foe it slays gives mana back and readies it sooner (seconds)
     at: 'wall'|'pair'|'path'  the entry's cd, cost and vs count only while the unit stands beside a wall ('wall'), beside
                       a unit of another kind ('pair'); 'path' with path: [k, cap]: vs +k for each path cell in its reach
     geom: { line, lineW, cone, zone }  positional shapes, read by spells that call spellGeom (below)
     pierce: k         each foe a piercing spell has already passed through adds +k to the next (spellPierceK)
   The hooks: abilities.js (byT, abReach, abCost, abCd, castAbility, the card's learn slot, save/load), game.js (hurt: spAmp
   and spRider; kill: spOnKill; resetTree: spForget), ui.js (the talents panel), meta.js and sim/bot.js (plans, the bot). */

const SP_LEARN_GOLD = [0, 0, 0];   // free (owner, 5 Nov 2026): taking a spell's talent teaches it to every unit of that kind at once, and to every one built later (spAutoLearn)
const SP_RIDE_GAP = 2;                // a rider lands on the same foe at most once every 2s per spell
const SP_GEOM_ABIL = { aimedshot: 1 };   // spells that read spellGeom / spellPierceK (spell-tune wires the rest)

