/* ================= ITEM LEVELS: an item's stats grow with the wave it was found on (force runs) =================
   docs/item_levels.md is the design. In short:
   - it.il, the Item Level: the wave an item dropped on (a wave boss's loot: the wave + IL.boss). Stamped where items are
     made (rollGear, the boss-loot panel's rnItem in ilvl_ui.js, the shop, the playtest), else the first time it is read.
   - its stat lines (itempower.js itemStats) are its rarity's budget x ilStatK: Damage and Spell Damage follow ilCurve, a
     typical unit's strike by wave; the percentage stats and mana grow gently (IL.pct); Range and Splash stay put. Its
     ability (Passive, Active) never changes with level.
   - it.rf, Rite-forged: the Rite it was found at (G.rite: a Chronicles location's rite), IL.rite more on every line a Rite.
   - level sync: an item works at most at the current wave + IL.boss (a warband's wave-50 gear in a new location's wave 1).
   - gold upgrades (relicUpgradeCost / upgradeRelic, in place of the hones): a level at a time up to the current wave,
     ilStepCost a level; it.upg is the gold spent (half comes back on salvage).
   - infusing (ilInfuse): a bag item fed into another lifts it to the fed item's level, and is used up.
   - sets (ilSetSync): while every piece of a set is held, all its pieces share the highest piece's level.
   Classic and Tower Wars (oldRules) never come here: ilOn() is false, and their relics keep hones and the power spike.
   Loaded after every other forces_*.js (the sets and epic sets), so the sim (sim/game_vm.js) has it too; the UI is
   ilvl_ui.js. Hooks: wrappers (rollGear, collectDrop, buyPlan, shopBuy, shopSellValue, restore, relicUpgradeCost,
   upgradeRelic), and itempower.js itemStats / itemCardHTML call ilStatK / ilCardBits. */

