/* ================= TUTORIAL: a short guided run of chapters =================
   Each chapter is a small scripted scenario on the field: a pre-set maze section, a one-line goal in a small coach card in
   the corner of the field (never a modal), a ring on the part of the screen it talks about, and a pass/fail check. The
   counter chapters bring one foe problem each: the field starts with the wrong answer, the wave is let through once, then
   the coach names the right answer, shows the foe's own info line and links the Spellbook entry for a fitting spell.
   It runs on the real game: newGame with a force commander, the waves through waveSpec/makeWave/spawn (wrapped so a
   chapter's wave is its own spec), the forecast's wave problem (waveProblem, wrapped), tryBuild, upgrade, the talent tree,
   the Bag and gear sheet, and the boss-loot panel. Nothing is saved but which chapters are done (localStorage TUT_KEY):
   no saved game, no scores, no play log, no campaign or challenge progress. Loaded last (build.sh): it wraps by name.
   The browser test is sim/tutorial_test.py; sim/tutorial_check.js plays every chapter's right path in a node vm. */
